QUIZ FILE SPEC
==============

A quiz file is UTF-8 text. The player is started with:

    python3 quiz.py path/to/quiz.txt

Comments and structure
----------------------
- A line whose first non-space character is "#" is a comment. Ignore it.
- Blank lines are ignored.
- Questions are separated by a line whose entire contents are "---".
- A final "---" after the last question is optional.
- Each question is a set of "KEY: value" lines.
- Split each line on the first ": " only. Values may contain colons.
- Every value is a single line.

Required fields
---------------
ID            Question id, kept as text. Used in the header and in remedial.txt.
TYPE          A short category such as "command" or "geography".
COMMAND       The subject of the question, shown above the prompt.
QUESTION      The prompt. The player appends " (choose 1-4 or other)".
1             First of the five real answers.
2             Second real answer.
3             Third real answer.
4             Fourth real answer.
5             Fifth real answer. This is not the Other control.
ANSWER        The correct answer, an integer 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5.
EXPLANATION   Shown after the user answers, whether right or wrong.

Optional fields
---------------
ACCEPT        Extra free-text answers, separated by " | ".
              The correct answer text is always accepted even if ACCEPT is omitted.
              Match rule: lowercase the user's text and collapse whitespace, then
              mark it correct if it contains any ACCEPT phrase treated the same way.
EXPLAINER     Text that must be shown before the choices. The user must check
              "I have read this" before Continue or Enter will open the question.
              Mouse wheel scrolls the explainer.

Display rules
-------------
- Question order is shuffled at start.
- For each question, one of the five answers is hidden at random and the other
  four are shown in random order as choices 1-4.
- The fifth on-screen control is always "Other (type your own answer)".
- If the hidden answer is the correct one, choices 1-4 are all wrong. The user
  must choose Other and type an accepted answer.
- If the correct answer is among the four shown, that choice is correct. Other
  is also correct when the typed text matches ACCEPT or the correct answer text.
- Keys 1-5, or a click, select a choice. In the Other box, Left, Right, Home,
  End, Backspace, and Delete edit at the cursor. Enter submits. Esc cancels Other.

Stop and remedial.txt
---------------------
- "Stop quiz" writes remedial.txt in the current directory and ends the run.
- That file contains every incorrect question, then every question not yet
  answered, including the current question if it has not been graded.
- Closing the window before the end does the same.
- Finishing the last question writes remedial.txt with incorrect questions only.
- remedial.txt uses this same format, with the original five answers and the
  original ANSWER, so it can be passed back to the player.

Window
------
- The window is resizable.
- Size and position are saved in quiz_window.json next to the program and
  restored on the next launch.

On loading
----------
If no files is given at the command line, the default_quiz.txt will be loaded.